# Lingua Franca

*Shared protocol for human-AI meaning transmission · bridges prose and AI-native processing*

---

## The Problem

```
human language → AI reads prose → reconstructs meaning → outputs prose
                  ↑ overhead every session · from scratch · implicit
```

LF is the response: a shared protocol both parties speak natively.
Not a replacement for human language — the operating layer underneath it.

---

## Two Layers

```
codons      unit language · concept + decoding context together
            AI loading a codon activates it · no reconstruction
            defined in: OPS/codons

density     transmission levels · same content · different receivers
            L1 for human reading cold · L3/L4 for AI-native transit
            defined in: COM/lingua.franca/conventions/conventions.density
```

---

## Density Levels

```
L1   .md      narrative      human cold · full prose · anyone
L2.5 .hybrid  working reg.   human + AI · emerges with shared context · densifies
L3   .fold    fold           AI-native · known instance · symbolic · no legend
L4   .codon   seed           portable · self-contained · carries legend · universal
```

L2.5 is not declared — it emerges. Not a skeleton — a register that densifies with intimacy.
L4 heavier than L3 but travels to any AI, any session, no prior context needed.

---

## The Conventions

```
conventions.density    when to use which level · receiver determines output
conventions.naming     [type].[subject].[format] · filename = identity
conventions.folding    how density levels apply when expressing a fold
```

---

## Position in CSOA

```
COM   language is agreed in communication → LF lives here
NAV   movement agreement depends on LF (fold as truth carrier)
OPS   codon system is LF's unit language
```

LF is substrate — agreed in COM, used everywhere.
What it is not: style guide, formatting preference, documentation convention.
It is the mechanism by which meaning survives transit.
